[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-overview-1600x120.png[/img]
Venworks Customizable HUD overhauls Starfield’s interface with customizable displays for combat, player status, equipment, environmental hazards, scanning, objectives, and nearby contacts.

The scanner identifies confirmed contacts and assigns them consistent codenames. The environment display shows your suit protection and active hazards, while the radar tracks detected contacts around your position.

This is a beta release. Previous HONKCORE themes remain available as legacy downloads in the Files section, but they are not compatible with this HUD and should not be installed alongside it.

[quote]
[size=4][b][u]New HUD and HONKCORE compatibility[/u][/b][/size]

This is a new custom HUD written from the ground up in Scaleform and ActionScript. It is not compatible with HONKCORE and has an expanded feature set.
[/quote]

[quote]
[size=4][b][u]Venworks Discord Community[/u][/b][/size]

’ve reopened the [url=https://discord.gg/DTbmrJDMxZ]Venworks Discord community[/url] as a central place for my mods, modding research, support, beta feedback, and bug reports. 

I’ll continue releasing my mods here on Nexus and through the Bethesda Game Studios Creations site (mostly for consoles), but recent site updates have made Nexus notifications and the Bugs and Posts sections less reliable.
[/quote]

[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-features-1600x120.png[/img]
[list]
[*]A configurable helmet frame with compass heading, threat state, active status effects, and Bethesda's current vehicle-exit control glyph.[/*]
[*]Player information for level, experience, health, oxygen, CO2, boost, carry mass, credits, digipicks, universal time, and a deterministic player serial.[/*]
[*]A passive equipment rail for all 12 favorite slots plus live weapon, ammunition, explosive, and power information.[/*]
[*]Planet and environment panels for location, local time, oxygen, temperature, gravity, suit protection, and active thermal, airborne, corrosive, and radiation categories.[/*]
[*]Environmental exposure bars that combine active Bethesda hazard categories, suit-protection depletion, and sustained player-O2 drain into modeled relative values. They are not real-world hazard measurements.[/*]
[*]A persistent tracked-objective panel.[/*]
[*]A full 360-degree contact radar for companions, parked ships, parked or recently exited vehicles, and acquired hostile contacts.[/*]
[*]A scanner-only 90-degree forward display that validates contacts, shows the nearest five, and assigns deterministic codenames for enemies, companions, ships, vehicles, positions, and other points of interest.[/*]
[*]Strict, atomic XML loading. Invalid or unsafe layout, palette, fragment, or SVG configuration prevents a partial custom HUD and displays a categorized diagnostic.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][u]Contact radar and scanner behavior[/u][/b][/size]

The radar maps contacts through the full 360 degrees around the player and displays companions, parked ships, parked or recently exited vehicles, and acquired hostile contacts up to 200 provider units away. The range uses Starfield's provider value and is not claimed to be meters.

Bethesda controls when hostile contacts are initially detected and delivered to the HUD. The radar does not discover unaware actors or act as a life-form detector. Once a hostile is acquired, it remains ranged and tracked until it moves beyond the radar's 200-unit limit.

The scanner panel is a separate forward-looking display. It validates contact data, sorts by distance, shows at most five contacts, and assigns stable display-only codenames such as enemy, companion, ship, vehicle, position, and POI identifiers. It does not consume actor names or invent random contacts.

[size=3][b][u]Beta platforms and feedback[/u][/b][/size]

The release targets PC and every console platform supported by Starfield Creations. Console testing and feedback are especially needed during the beta. Large-HUD, ultrawide, and radar-transition feedback is also welcome.

[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-overview-1600x120.png[/img]

[size=3][b][u]Release themes[/u][/b][/size]

Four separately distributed variants choose different starting palettes. Enable only one variant at a time. Every new variant includes all five stock palettes, so PC players can switch the active palette without reinstalling the HUD.

[list]
[*][b]Venworks Customizable HUD - Venworks Theme[/b] — starts with [font=Courier New]venworks.xml[/font].[/*]
[*][b]Venworks Customizable HUD - Trackers Alliance Theme[/b] — starts with [font=Courier New]trackers-alliance.xml[/font].[/*]
[*][b]Venworks Customizable HUD - Freestar Collective Theme[/b] — starts with [font=Courier New]freestar-collective.xml[/font].[/*]
[*][b]Venworks Customizable HUD - Crimson Fleet Theme[/b] — starts with [font=Courier New]crimson-fleet.xml[/font].[/*]
[/list]

The additional neutral option is [font=Courier New]starfield.xml[/font].

[size=3][b][u]XML customization[/u][/b][/size]

Versioned XML controls layout, visibility, colors, typography, meters, icons, reusable component fragments, and approved Bethesda HUD sections. Start with the [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui/blob/master/docs/USER_CONFIGURATION.md]user configuration guide[/url], then use the complete [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui/blob/master/docs/LAYOUT_CONFIGURATION_REFERENCE.md]layout reference[/url] and [url=https://github.com/monster-cookie/venworks-honkcore-ta-ui/blob/master/docs/PALETTE_CONFIGURATION_REFERENCE.md]palette reference[/url].

A .NET WYSIWYG application for creating and modifying themes is a long-term roadmap item. It is not included in this beta.

[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-installation-instructions-1600x120.png[/img]
[size=3][b][u]Via Vortex or Mod Organizer 2[/u][/b][/size]

Install one new theme variant as you would any other Starfield mod. Let it win the intended conflicts for [font=Courier New]hudmenu.gfx[/font], [font=Courier New]hudmenu_lrg.gfx[/font], and [font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI[/font]. Do not enable more than one new theme variant.

[size=3][b][u]Manually[/u][/b][/size]

A mod manager is strongly recommended because it makes file conflicts, updates, and recovery safer. For a manual installation, copy the package's [font=Courier New]Interface[/font] directory into [font=Courier New]<Starfield installation directory>\Data[/font]. Back up files before overwriting them.

[size=3][b][u]Change the active color palette on PC[/u][/b][/size]

[list=1]
[*]Enable only one Venworks Customizable HUD release variant.[/*]
[*]Fully exit Starfield.[/*]
[*]Back up the complete active [font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI[/font] directory. Mod-manager updates, reinstalls, purge/deploy operations, and conflict changes can overwrite local XML edits.[/*]
[*]Open [font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI\layout.xml[/font] in a plain-text or XML editor.[/*]
[*]Find the root [font=Courier New]<venworksCUI>[/font] element and change only its [font=Courier New]palette[/font] attribute. For example: [font=Courier New]palette="trackers-alliance.xml"[/font].[/*]
[*]Choose one packaged filename: [font=Courier New]venworks.xml[/font], [font=Courier New]trackers-alliance.xml[/font], [font=Courier New]freestar-collective.xml[/font], [font=Courier New]crimson-fleet.xml[/font], or [font=Courier New]starfield.xml[/font].[/*]
[*]The filename must refer directly to one XML file under [font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI\palettes[/font]. Subdirectories, path traversal, URLs, query strings, and fragments are rejected.[/*]
[*]Save the file and fully restart Starfield. Live palette switching is not supported.[/*]
[/list]

The safest long-term PC setup is a small personal override mod containing the customized [font=Courier New]Interface\VenworksCUI[/font] files and loading after the selected release variant. Console players should install the Creation whose title matches the starting palette they want.

[img]https://cdn.venworkscreations.com/NexusMods/description-divider-known-issues-1600x120.png[/img]
[list]
[*]This is a beta release.[/*]
[*]The configurable release covers the on-foot player HUD. Ship UI remains outside the current release.[/*]
[*]The radar is an acquired-contact display, not a life-form detector. Neutral creatures and unaware potential hostiles are not guaranteed to appear.[/*]
[*]Palette and other XML changes require a complete Starfield restart; live reload is unsupported.[/*]
[*]Do not combine this HUD with HONKCORE or another mod that replaces the same HUD movies unless a purpose-built compatibility patch explicitly combines their changes.[/*]
[/list]

[size=3][b][u]Legacy HONKCORE files[/u][/b][/size]

The previous HONKCORE theme downloads will remain in the Files section for players who want the older release. Those legacy files still require HONKCORE and are not upgrades, requirements, or companions for Venworks Customizable HUD. Install either a legacy HONKCORE theme or one new customizable HUD theme, never both.

